    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily owner-registration limit: creating an owner is now rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already have today's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`DailyRegistrationLimitException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` signaling the daily cap was reached, mirroring the existing `CityAtCapacityException` pattern.\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping the new exception to `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` with `{\"errors\": [\"registrationDate\"]}`.\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after the required-fields check, counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count is \u2265 100 (owners default to today's date on creation).\n\nBoth the new acceptance test (`coreRejectsOverDailyLimit`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
